- description: Upstream Actions queries whose findings ABOM records and attributes

# ABOM reaches no security conclusion of its own, so this suite may only ever *select*
# upstream queries. Every result keeps the `@id` of the query that produced it, and that rule
# id is the whole basis of the verdict downstream. Adding a query written here would make ABOM
# the author of a finding it also reports, which the model has no way to represent.
#
# This is deliberately the same 35 queries as the upstream suite it replaces, so that owning
# the file changes nothing on the day it lands. Filters belong below, one reviewable diff at a
# time.
#
# Pinned exactly rather than by range: without `version:` the CLI resolves the most recent pack,
# so the set of rules ABOM attributes could change with no commit here.
- import: codeql-suites/actions-all.qls
  from: codeql/actions-queries
  version: 0.6.35

# The nine `experimental/` queries stay in. Precision is a property of the rule, and ABOM
# attributes rather than adjudicates: a consumer filtering on rule id can always drop them,
# whereas a finding never collected cannot be recovered.
